    5 => ['title'=>'PM Awas Yojana Urban', 'content'=>'<p>Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana Urban (PMAY-U) is a central government housing scheme launched in June 2015 by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs. The scheme aims to provide pucca houses with basic amenities to all eligible urban households by 2024. It addresses the housing needs of the urban poor including the Economically Weaker Section (EWS), Lower Income Group (LIG) and Middle Income Group (MIG) categories through different verticals of assistance.</p><h2>Four Verticals of PMAY-U</h2><p>The scheme operates through four components: In-Situ Slum Redevelopment (ISSR), Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS), Affordable Housing in Partnership (AHP) and Beneficiary Led Individual House Construction (BLIHC). Each vertical targets a specific segment of the urban population with different subsidy amounts and conditions.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>Applicant families should not own a pucca house anywhere in India. The family should belong to EWS (annual income up to Rs 3 lakh), LIG (Rs 3-6 lakh) or MIG (Rs 6-18 lakh) categories. The scheme is open to all castes, religions and communities. Women ownership or joint ownership is mandatory for EWS and LIG categories. The beneficiary family should not have availed housing subsidy from any other government scheme.</p><h2>Benefits and Subsidy</h2><p>Under CLSS, interest subsidy ranges from 3% to 6.5% on home loans depending on the income category. EWS and LIG get 6.5% subsidy on loans up to Rs 6 lakh. MIG-I gets 4% subsidy on loans up to Rs 9 lakh. MIG-II gets 3% subsidy on loans up to Rs 12 lakh. Under AHP and BLIHC, direct financial assistance of up to Rs 1.5 lakh per house is provided for construction or enhancement.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Eligible beneficiaries can apply through the official PMAY-U website pmay-urban.gov.in or visit their local municipal corporation or urban local body office. The online portal allows registration, document upload and tracking of application status. Beneficiaries need to provide Aadhaar, income certificate and house ownership documents.</p><h2>Required Documents</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card of all family members</li><li>Income certificate from competent authority</li><li>Address proof</li><li>Bank account details for subsidy transfer</li><li>Photograph of existing house</li><li>Property documents if applicable</li></ul>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Urban households belonging to EWS (income up to Rs 3 lakh), LIG (Rs 3-6 lakh) or MIG (Rs 6-18 lakh). No pucca house anywhere in India. Women ownership mandatory for EWS/LIG. Not availed other housing subsidy.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Interest subsidy of 3% to 6.5% on home loans. Direct assistance up to Rs 1.5 lakh for house construction. Subsidy amount varies by income category. Four different verticals for different needs.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Visit pmay-urban.gov.in or local municipal corporation office. Register with Aadhaar and income details. Upload required documents. Track application status online. Subsidy directly credited to bank account.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>Address Proof</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>House Photograph</li><li>Property Documents</li></ul>'
    ],
    198 => ['title'=>'PM Gramin Sadak Yojana Phase 3', 'content'=>'<p>Pradhan Mantri Gramin Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) is a flagship central government scheme launched in 2000 by the Ministry of Rural Development. The scheme aims to provide all-weather road connectivity to unconnected habitations in rural areas. PMGSY Phase III was launched in 2019 with a focus on consolidating the existing rural road network by upgrading priority roads to improve rural infrastructure and economic development.</p><h2>Objectives</h2><p>The primary objective of PMGSY Phase III is to provide all-weather road connectivity to unconnected habitations with population of 500+ in plain areas and 250+ in hilly/tribal areas. The scheme also focuses on upgrading existing rural roads to higher standards and ensuring proper drainage and road safety features.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Habitations with population of 500 or more in plain areas and 250 or more in hilly, desert and tribal areas are eligible. The scheme covers all states and union territories of India. Priority is given to unconnected habitations in backward and tribal districts.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>All-weather road connectivity improves access to markets, schools, hospitals and other essential services. It reduces transportation costs for agricultural produce and enables better economic opportunities for rural communities.</p><h2>Implementation</h2><p>The scheme is implemented by the Rural Roads Development Agency at the state level. Local communities are involved in planning and monitoring through the Gram Panchayat.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Rural habitations with population 500+ (plain) or 250+ (hilly/tribal). All states and UTs covered. Priority to backward and tribal districts.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>All-weather road connectivity. Better access to markets, schools, hospitals. Reduced transport costs. Economic development of rural areas.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Implemented through state Rural Roads Development Agencies. Local Gram Panchayats identify unconnected habitations and submit proposals to the district planning committee.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Gram Panchayat resolution</li><li>Habitation population data</li><li>Land availability certificate</li></ul>'
    ],
    264 => ['title'=>'Mukhyamantri Kisan Kalyan Yojana MP', 'content'=>'<p>Mukhyamantri Kisan Kalyan Yojana is a state government scheme launched by the Government of Madhya Pradesh under the Department of Farmer Welfare and Agriculture Development. The scheme provides a state government top-up of Rs 4,000 per year to farmers of Madhya Pradesh over and above the central PM-KISAN amount of Rs 6,000. This means eligible farmers in MP receive a total of Rs 10,000 per year from both schemes combined.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All farmers registered under PM-KISAN in Madhya Pradesh are automatically eligible. The scheme covers small and marginal farmers who own less than 2 hectares of cultivable land. Farmers from all castes, religions and communities are eligible. The scheme is administered through the state agriculture department.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Rs 4,000 per year as state top-up to PM-KISAN beneficiaries. Combined with central Rs 6,000, total benefit is Rs 10,000 per year. The amount is transferred directly to the bank account through DBT in installments matching the PM-KISAN schedule.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>No separate application is needed for farmers already registered under PM-KISAN in Madhya Pradesh. The state government uses the same beneficiary database as PM-KISAN. New farmers can register through the PM-KISAN portal pmkisan.gov.in or visit their local agriculture office.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>PM-KISAN registered farmers in Madhya Pradesh. Small and marginal farmers with less than 2 hectares. All castes and communities eligible.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Rs 4,000 per year state top-up. Combined with PM-KISAN makes Rs 10,000/year. DBT to bank account. Same schedule as central installments.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Automatic for PM-KISAN beneficiaries in MP. New farmers register through PM-KISAN portal or local agriculture office. State government syncs data with central database.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>PM-KISAN Registration Number</li></ul>'
    ],
    266 => ['title'=>'Mukhyamantri Teerth Darshan Yojana MP', 'content'=>'<p>Mukhyamantri Teerth Darshan Yojana is a pilgrimage scheme launched by the Government of Madhya Pradesh under the Department of Social Justice and Empowerment. The scheme provides free pilgrimage tours to selected religious places for senior citizens of the state. The objective is to enable elderly citizens who cannot afford pilgrimage travel to visit important religious sites and fulfill their spiritual aspirations.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Senior citizens aged 60 years and above who are permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh are eligible. Priority is given to BPL families and those from SC, ST and OBC communities. Beneficiaries should not have availed the benefit earlier. The scheme covers both government and private sector retirees.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Free pilgrimage tour covering transportation, accommodation, food and religious offerings. Popular destinations include Ram Janmabhoomi Ayodhya, Kashi Vishwanath, Tirupati, Puri Jagannath and other major religious sites in India. An attendant is also provided for senior citizens who need assistance.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Eligible senior citizens can apply through the District Social Justice Office or through the Madhya Pradesh government portal. Applications require basic personal details, age proof and residence certificate. Selection is done on a first-come-first-served basis with priority to specific categories.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Senior citizens 60+ years. Permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh. Priority to BPL, SC/ST/OBC. Not availed benefit previously.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Free pilgrimage tour including transport, accommodation and food. Major religious destinations covered. Attendant for needy senior citizens. Group tours with medical support.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply at District Social Justice Office or MP government portal. Submit age proof and residence certificate. Wait for selection and tour schedule.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Age Proof</li><li>Residence Certificate</li><li>BPL Certificate if applicable</li><li>Passport size photograph</li></ul>'
    ],
    267 => ['title'=>'Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana MP', 'content'=>'<p>Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) in Madhya Pradesh is implemented jointly by the state and central governments to provide affordable housing to all eligible households in the state. The scheme covers both urban and rural areas of MP. The state government supplements the central assistance with additional state-specific benefits to accelerate housing coverage in the state.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Families identified as houseless or living in kutcha houses in Madhya Pradesh are eligible. The scheme covers EWS, LIG and MIG categories in urban areas and all rural households listed in SECC 2011. Priority to SC, ST, OBC, minority communities and women-headed households. Beneficiaries should not own a pucca house anywhere in India.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Financial assistance of up to Rs 1.20-1.30 lakh for rural areas and interest subsidy of 3% to 6.5% on home loans for urban areas. The state government provides additional support for landless families by facilitating land allotment. Houses include basic amenities like toilet, electricity and water supply.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Houseless or kutcha house dwellers in MP. EWS/LIG/MIG in urban areas. SECC 2011 listed in rural areas. SC/ST/OBC/minority priority. Women-headed households preference.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Financial assistance of Rs 1.20-1.30 lakh. Interest subsidy on home loans. Basic amenities included. State support for landless families.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply through Gram Panchayat (rural) or municipal corporation (urban). SECC database verification. Gram Sabha approval. Fund release in installments based on construction progress.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>BPL/SECC Certificate</li><li>Land Document</li><li>Bank Account</li><li>House Photograph</li></ul>'
    ],
    268 => ['title'=>'Medhavi Chatravritti Yojana MP Scholarship', 'content'=>'<p>Medhavi Chatravritti Yojana is a merit scholarship scheme launched by the Government of Madhya Pradesh under the Department of School Education. The scheme provides financial assistance to meritorious students of the state pursuing higher and professional education. The objective is to encourage academic excellence and ensure that financial constraints do not prevent talented students from accessing quality education.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Students who are permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh and have secured high marks in Class 10, 12 or graduation examinations are eligible. The scheme covers students pursuing higher secondary, undergraduate, postgraduate and professional courses. Family income should be below the threshold set by the government. Students should have at least 60% marks in the qualifying examination.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Scholarship amount varies based on the course and level of study. Tuition fees and maintenance allowance are covered for the entire duration of the course. The scholarship is renewed annually based on academic performance with minimum 60% marks in the previous year.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>MP domicile students with 60%+ marks in qualifying exam. Pursuing higher/professional education. Family income below specified threshold. Annual renewal requires 60%+ marks.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Tuition fee coverage. Maintenance allowance. Annual renewal based on performance. Covers higher secondary to professional courses.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply through MP scholarship portal or district education office. Submit marksheets, income certificate and domicile certificate. Selection based on merit. Amount credited to bank account.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Marksheets</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>Domicile Certificate</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Institution Fee Structure</li></ul>'
    ],
    272 => ['title'=>'Ladli Laxmi Yojana MP Girl Child Scheme', 'content'=>'<p>Ladli Laxmi Yojana is a flagship girl child welfare scheme launched by the Government of Madhya Pradesh in 2007 under the Department of Women and Child Development. The scheme aims to improve the status of the girl child in society by providing financial support for her education and marriage. It addresses the issue of declining child sex ratio and promotes education among girls in the state.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>The scheme is applicable to girls born in Madhya Pradesh after January 1, 2006. The family should be permanent residents of MP. Parents annual income should not exceed Rs 1.5 lakh. The scheme covers families from all castes and communities. Maximum two girl children per family are covered.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Financial bonds of Rs 6,000 are purchased in the name of the girl child at birth. The bond matures when the girl turns 21 years, providing a lump sum amount of approximately Rs 1-2 lakh depending on the accumulated interest. Partial amounts can be withdrawn at various education milestones - Class 6, Class 9, Class 11 and Class 12 - to support education expenses. Additional benefits for girls who remain unmarried until 21 and complete their education.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>The application is submitted at the time of birth registration at the local Janpad Panchayat or municipal corporation. Parents need to provide the birth certificate, residence proof and income certificate. The bond is issued in the girls name and managed by the district womens development office.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Girls born in MP after 2006. Family income below Rs 1.5 lakh per year. Two girl children per family maximum. Permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Rs 6,000 bond at birth matures at age 21. Withdrawals at education milestones. Lump sum of Rs 1-2 lakh at maturity. Additional benefits for unmarried educated girls.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply at birth registration in Janpad Panchayat or municipal corporation. Submit birth certificate, income proof and residence proof. Bond issued in girls name managed by district office.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Birth Certificate</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>Residence Proof</li><li>Parents Aadhaar</li></ul>'
    ],
    275 => ['title'=>'Ayushman Bharat Niramaya MP', 'content'=>'<p>Ayushman Bharat Niramaya is a health insurance scheme implemented by the Government of Madhya Pradesh in collaboration with the central Ayushman Bharat PMJAY scheme. The scheme provides health coverage to eligible families in Madhya Pradesh for secondary and tertiary hospitalization. It extends the benefits of the national scheme to the states eligible population with state-specific enhancements.</p><h2>Coverage</h2><p>The scheme provides cashless health coverage of up to Rs 5 lakh per family per year. Coverage includes hospitalization, surgeries, diagnostic tests and medicines. Pre-existing diseases are covered from day one. Treatment is available at empaneled government and private hospitals across MP and other states.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Families identified through the SECC database in Madhya Pradesh are eligible. The scheme covers deprived rural families and specified occupation categories in urban areas. All family members are covered including newborns and dependent parents. There is no age limit for coverage.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>SECC identified families in Madhya Pradesh. Deprived rural and specified urban occupation categories. All family members covered. No age limit.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Cashless health cover up to Rs 5 lakh per family per year. Pre-existing diseases covered from day one. Treatment at empaneled hospitals across India.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Check eligibility at pmjay.gov.in. Visit empaneled hospital with Aadhaar. Hospital verifies and provides cashless treatment. No physical card required.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Ration Card</li><li>SECC Inclusion Proof</li></ul>'
    ],
    276 => ['title'=>'Kanyashree Prakalpa West Bengal', 'content'=>'<p>Kanyashree Prakalpa is a flagship girl child welfare scheme launched by the Government of West Bengal in 2013 under the Department of Women Development and Social Welfare. The scheme aims to improve the status of girls by providing conditional cash transfers to prevent child marriage and promote education. It has received international recognition including the United Nations Public Service Award.</p><h2>Two Components</h2><p>The scheme has two components: K1 provides an annual scholarship of Rs 1,000 to girls aged 13-18 who are unmarried and attending school. K2 provides a one-time grant of Rs 25,000 to girls on their 18th birthday who are unmarried and have completed certain education milestones. Both components encourage girls to stay in school and delay marriage.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Girls aged 13-18 years who are permanent residents of West Bengal are eligible. They must be unmarried and enrolled in educational institutions. Family income should be below Rs 1.2 lakh per year for K1 and Rs 1.5 lakh for K2. Regular attendance of at least 75% is required.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>K1 provides Rs 1,000 annual scholarship for school expenses. K2 provides Rs 25,000 one-time grant at age 18 for higher education or skill training. The scheme has benefited over 4 million girls in West Bengal and significantly reduced child marriage rates in the state.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Girls 13-18 years, West Bengal residents, unmarried, enrolled in school. Family income below Rs 1.2 lakh (K1) or Rs 1.5 lakh (K2). Minimum 75% attendance.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>K1: Rs 1,000 annual scholarship. K2: Rs 25,000 one-time grant at age 18. Prevents child marriage. Promotes girl education. Over 4 million beneficiaries.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply through school or local government office. Submit birth certificate, income certificate and school enrollment proof. Applications verified by district authorities. Benefits transferred to bank account.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Birth Certificate</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>School Enrollment Proof</li><li>Bank Account</li><li>Residence Proof</li></ul>'
    ],
    282 => ['title'=>'Krishak Bandhu West Bengal', 'content'=>'<p>Krishak Bandhu is a farmer welfare scheme launched by the Government of West Bengal under the Department of Agriculture. The scheme provides financial assistance and social security to farmers in the state. It includes two main components: a direct cash transfer of Rs 2,000 per acre per year to farmers and a life insurance cover for the head of the farming family.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All farmers who are permanent residents of West Bengal and own agricultural land are eligible. The scheme covers farmers with any landholding size. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid records are also eligible. The farmer should be the head of the family or the primary earning member engaged in agriculture.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Direct cash transfer of Rs 2,000 per acre per year (subject to a maximum of 2 acres). The amount is paid in two installments coinciding with the kharif and rabi seasons. Additionally, life insurance cover of Rs 2 lakh is provided to the head of the farming family in case of accidental death or permanent disability.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Farmers can register through the official Krishak Bandhu portal or visit their local agriculture office or block development office. The application requires land records, Aadhaar card and bank account details. After verification, the farmer receives a Krishak Bandhu card and the benefits are transferred to the bank account.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>West Bengal farmers with agricultural land. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers eligible. Any landholding size. Must be head of farming family engaged in agriculture.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Rs 2,000 per acre per year (max 2 acres). Two installments per crop season. Life insurance of Rs 2 lakh for accidental death/disability.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Register on Krishak Bandhu portal or visit agriculture office. Submit land records, Aadhaar and bank details. Verification by agriculture department. Benefits credited to bank account.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Passport Photo</li></ul>'
    ],
    286 => ['title'=>'Gatidhara West Bengal Transport Subsidy', 'content'=>'<p>Gatidhara is a transport subsidy scheme launched by the Government of West Bengal under the Department of Transport. The scheme provides financial assistance to students from economically weaker sections for their commuting expenses. It aims to reduce the financial burden of transportation on students and encourage them to continue their education without being hindered by distance or travel costs.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>Students from economically weaker families who are permanent residents of West Bengal are eligible. The scheme covers students studying in government and government-aided schools, colleges and universities. Family income should be below the threshold specified by the state government. Students must have regular attendance and good academic standing.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Subsidized or free bus passes for students to commute between their residence and educational institution. The subsidy covers the cost of public transport including state-run buses. The scheme significantly reduces the monthly transportation expenses for students from low-income families.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>Economically weaker students in West Bengal. Government/government-aided institutions. Family income below state threshold. Regular attendance required.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Subsidized bus passes. Free public transport for eligible students. Reduced monthly commuting expenses. Covers school to university level.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply through educational institution or transport department office. Submit income certificate and student ID. Bus pass issued after verification by concerned authorities.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Student ID Card</li><li>Income Certificate</li><li>Residence Proof</li><li>Passport Photo</li></ul>'
    ],
