    2 => ['title'=>'PM Fasal Bima Yojana PMFBY', 'content'=>'<p>Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) is a flagship crop insurance scheme launched in 2016 by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare. The scheme provides affordable crop insurance to farmers against crop failure due to natural calamities, pests and diseases. It aims to stabilize farm income and encourage farmers to adopt modern agricultural practices by reducing their financial risk.</p><h2>Coverage</h2><p>The scheme covers all food crops, oilseeds and annual commercial or horticultural crops. It provides coverage against yield losses due to natural fire, lightning, storm, hailstorm, cyclone, typhoon, flood, inundation, drought, dry spells, pests and diseases. Post-harvest losses are also covered for up to 14 days.</p><h2>Premium</h2><p>The premium rates are very affordable: 2% of sum insured for Kharif crops, 1.5% for Rabi crops and 5% for annual commercial or horticultural crops. The difference between the premium paid by farmers and the actual premium is shared by the central and state governments.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All farmers who have a loan from financial institutions are covered compulsorily. Non-loanee farmers can also voluntarily enroll. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records are eligible.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>All farmers including loanee and non-loanee. Tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records eligible. All types of crops covered.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Insurance coverage at nominal premium (2% Kharif, 1.5% Rabi, 5% commercial). Covers yield losses from natural calamities, pests, diseases. Post-harvest loss coverage for 14 days.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Loanee farmers automatically covered through their lending institution. Non-loanee farmers can enroll through Common Service Centres (CSC) or bank branches before the cut-off date for each season.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Crop Sowing Details</li></ul>'
    ],
    3 => ['title'=>'Kisan Credit Card KCC', 'content'=>'<p>Kisan Credit Card (KCC) scheme was launched in 1998 by the Government of India to provide affordable credit to farmers for their agricultural needs. The scheme is implemented by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare through banks. It provides farmers with timely access to credit for crop production, post-harvest expenses, farm maintenance, dairy and fisheries activities, and other agricultural purposes. The scheme has played a crucial role in reducing farmers dependence on informal money lenders and improving access to institutional credit.</p><h2>Features and Benefits</h2><p>The scheme provides a credit card with a pre-approved limit based on land holding, crop pattern and credit history. Farmers can withdraw cash as needed and pay interest only on the amount used, making it a flexible and cost-effective solution. The card is valid for 5 years with annual renewal, providing continuous access to credit without repeated paperwork. Interest rates are affordable at 7% per annum with an additional 3% subvention for farmers who repay on time, bringing the effective interest rate down to just 4%. This makes it one of the cheapest sources of agricultural credit in India.</p><h2>Coverage and Limits</h2><p>The scheme covers all types of farmers including small, marginal, tenant and sharecroppers. Individual farmers, joint farmers and farmer groups are all eligible. Loans up to Rs 3 lakh are provided with no collateral requirement for loans up to Rs 1.60 lakh. The credit limit is assessed based on the farmers land holding, cropping pattern and scale of farming activities. Personal accident insurance cover of Rs 1 lakh is also provided to cardholders at nominal premium.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>All farmers including small and marginal farmers, tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records are eligible for the scheme. Individual farmers, joint farmers and farmer producer organizations can apply. Farmers engaged in crop production, dairy farming, fisheries, poultry and other allied activities are covered. There is no upper limit on land holding size for eligibility.</p><h2>Application Process</h2><p>Farmers can apply at any bank branch with their land records and identity proof. The bank assesses the credit limit based on land holding and crop pattern. The assessment takes into account the cost of cultivation, maintenance expenses and family needs. Once approved, the Kisan Credit Card is issued within 15 to 30 days. Farmers can also apply through Common Service Centres and online banking portals.</p><h2>Required Documents</h2><ul><li>Aadhaar Card for identity verification</li><li>Land records or cultivation proof</li><li>Bank account details for loan disbursement</li><li>Passport size photograph</li><li>Crop plan for the upcoming season</li><li>Previous loan repayment history if applicable</li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Can tenant farmers apply for KCC?</h3><p>Yes, tenant farmers and sharecroppers with valid land records or cultivation certificates are eligible.</p><h3>What is the interest rate on KCC?</h3><p>The interest rate is 7% per annum. Farmers who repay on time get an additional 3% subvention, making the effective rate 4%.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>All farmers including small, marginal, tenant and sharecroppers. Individual and joint farmers. Farmer producer organizations. Farmers engaged in crop, dairy, fisheries and allied activities.</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>Credit up to Rs 3 lakh at 7% interest. 3% subvention for timely repayment (4% effective rate). No collateral up to Rs 1.60 lakh. Personal accident insurance Rs 1 lakh. 5 year validity with annual renewal.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply at any bank branch with land records and identity proof. Bank assesses credit limit based on land holding and crop pattern. Card issued within 15-30 days after verification of documents and credit assessment.</p>',
        'required_documents'=>'<ul><li>Aadhaar Card</li><li>Land Records</li><li>Bank Account Details</li><li>Passport Photo</li><li>Crop Plan</li></ul>'
    ],
    8 => ['title'=>'MGNREGA Job Guarantee', 'content'=>'<p>Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) is a landmark social security scheme launched in 2005 by the Ministry of Rural Development. The scheme guarantees 100 days of wage employment per year to every rural household whose adult members volunteer for unskilled manual work. It is one of the largest work guarantee programs in the world.</p><h2>Key Features</h2><p>Employment is provided within 15 days of application. If employment is not provided, unemployment allowance must be paid. Wages are paid as per the minimum wage rate fixed by the central government, with different rates for different states. At least one-third of workers must be women.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>All rural households are eligible. Adult members (18+ years) who are willing to do unskilled manual work can apply. Both men and women are eligible. No minimum education requirement.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>100 days guaranteed employment per household per year. Wages paid weekly through DBT. Works include water conservation, drought proofing, flood control, rural connectivity and land development. Worksite facilities include drinking water, shade and first aid.</p>',
        'eligibility'=>'<p>All adult rural household members (18+ years). Willing to do unskilled manual work. No education requirement. Priority to women (33% reservation).</p>',
        'benefits'=>'<p>100 days work per year per household. Weekly wage payment via DBT. Unemployment allowance if work not provided within 15 days. Worksite facilities provided.</p>',
        'application_process'=>'<p>Apply at local Gram Panchayat office. Fill Form A with basic details. Job Card issued within 15 days. Submit work request when employment needed.</p>',
